invariant: INV-7
file: handshake_parser.c
catches: webpki_session_aes
builds: bin/webpki_session_aes
reason: the two-suite client accepts TLS_AES_256_GCM_SHA384 in a ServerHello
  although its ClientHello listed ChaCha20 and AES-128-GCM alone, which RFC
  9846 section 4.2.3 makes an illegal_parameter. The client would key a
  suite it never agreed to run, with a 16-byte key where that suite
  derives 32.

--- old
    return suite == SUITE_CHACHA20_POLY1305_SHA256 || suite == SUITE_AES_128_GCM_SHA256;
--- new
    return suite == SUITE_CHACHA20_POLY1305_SHA256 || suite == SUITE_AES_128_GCM_SHA256 ||
           suite == 0x1302;
